add('Frontend technology stack',head('THE BROWSER LAYER','React renders the learning experience')+'<div class="grid">'+card('react','React + TypeScript','Components and state<br>Lesson navigation and tabs<br>Typed messages and results')+card('vite','Vite','Development server<br>React tooling<br>Local /api proxy')+card('assets','CSS + static assets','Layouts and themes<br>Illustrations and infographics<br>Included audio and learning content')+'</div><div class="banner"><p>GitHub main · 7717a10 · package.json ranges and package-lock.json resolutions checked.</p></div>',[('react','React renders the interface, while TypeScript describes the data and component contracts. State updates drive prompts, progress frames, and results.'),('vite','Vite serves the frontend during development and proxies API requests to Express. The browser normally opens the frontend, not the backend port.'),('assets','CSS, illustrations, infographics, and audio shape the learning experience. These assets support the interface; they do not execute the remote agent loop.')],['package.json','vite.config.ts','src/components/LessonWorkspace.tsx'])
add('Backend technology stack',head('THE HOST LAYER','Node and Express own application execution')+'<div class="grid">'+card('node','Node 24+ + tsx','Node runs the host process<br>tsx loads TypeScript in development<br>Express 5 routes HTTP requests')+card('zod','Zod contracts','Parse input before execution<br>Validate streamed progress<br>Validate the terminal result')+card('sdk','Anthropic TypeScript SDK','Server-side client<br>Managed sessions and events<br>Provider access and cleanup')+'</div><div class="banner"><p>Locked stack: React 19.3.0 · Vite 8.3.4 · Express 5.3.0 · TypeScript 7.0.2 · SDK 1.3.0</p></div>',[('node','The project requires Node twenty-four or later. Its development supervisor starts the TypeScript backend through tsx, and Express handles the local HTTP routes.'),('zod','Zod validates values at runtime. TypeScript types help during development, but a network request still needs runtime validation before it can start work.'),('sdk','The backend uses the Anthropic TypeScript SDK to access Managed Agents. Credentials stay in the server environment. The direct Anthropic SDK is pinned to one point three point zero on GitHub main. Exact package resolutions are recorded in its lockfile.')],['package.json','scripts/dev-server.mjs','server/lib/managed-config.ts'])

