def detail(n,text,code,label,spoken1,spoken2,refs,active):
 body=head(f'STEP {n} OF 8 · IMPLEMENTATION',steps[n-1])+'<div class="two"><div>'+cue(f'step-{n}-explain','<p>'+text+'</p>')+'</div><div class="code"><div class="label">'+label+'</div>'+cue(f'step-{n}-code','<pre>'+html.escape(code)+'</pre>')+'</div></div><div class="rail">'+''.join((f'<span class="arrow">→</span>' if i else '')+f'<b class="{"on" if i in active else ""}">{t}</b>' for i,t in enumerate(['React browser','Vite proxy','Express host','Managed runtime']))+'</div>'
 add(steps[n-1],body,[(f'step-{n}-explain',spoken1),(f'step-{n}-code',spoken2)],refs)
detail(1,'npm run dev starts the supervised backend and Vite together.<br><br>Default frontend: 5174<br>Default backend: 3076<br><br>Use the address printed by Vite if the preferred port is busy.', '"dev": "concurrently --kill-others ..."\n"dev:server": "node scripts/dev-server.mjs"\n"dev:web": "vite"\n\n// server/index.ts\napp.listen(port, "127.0.0.1");','package.json + server/index.ts · excerpts; dev command abbreviated','The first step is local startup. The development command starts both sides, while the backend supervisor restarts its child when relevant source files change.','The package scripts launch the supervisor and Vite. Express binds to the local loopback address. The frontend normally uses port fifty-one seventy-four and the backend uses thirty seventy-six.', ['package.json','scripts/dev-server.mjs','server/index.ts','vite.config.ts'],[1,2])
detail(2,'React keeps the prompt, pending state, progress frames and result.<br><br>A new run clears old output and creates an AbortController for that request.', 'const request = new AbortController();\ncontroller.current = request;\nsetPending(true);\nsetFrames([]);\nsetResult(undefined);','src/concepts/Concept01Query.tsx · excerpt','React prepares one run by collecting the prompt and resetting the display. Keeping pending state, progress frames, and the final result separate makes the interface easier to reason about.','An AbortController belongs to this request. It can stop local waiting, but by itself it cannot prove that remote work stopped. The backend has separate cleanup responsibilities.', ['src/concepts/Concept01Query.tsx'],[0])
detail(3,'streamPost uses fetch with POST.<br><br>Vite proxies /api to Express during development.<br><br>The response is an event stream, not one immediate JSON document.', 'await streamPost("/api/c1/query",\n  { mode: chosen, prompt,\n    ...(chosen === "scripted"\n      ? { scenario } : {}) },\n  { signal: request.signal,\n    idleMs: 25_000, deadlineMs: 150_000,\n    resultSchema: lab01ResultSchema,\n    onEvent });','Concept01Query.tsx · excerpt; callback referenced by name','The browser sends a JSON request through the local API proxy. It then reads the response incrementally as server-sent events.','This helper uses fetch because the operation is a POST. The native EventSource interface is designed around GET. Idle and overall deadlines bound browser waiting, and the result schema validates the terminal payload.', ['src/concepts/Concept01Query.tsx','src/lib/sse.ts','vite.config.ts'],[0,1])
detail(4,'The route validates input before provider access.<br><br>It enforces local request rules, concurrency and deadlines.<br><br>openSse prepares progress, error and result frames.', 'const parsed = lab01RequestSchema\n  .safeParse(request.body);\nif (!parsed.success) {\n  response.status(400).json(\n    apiError("INVALID_REQUEST",\n      "Check the prompt and mode.", parsed.error));\n  return;\n}','server/concepts/01-query.ts · excerpt','Express receives the request and validates it before selecting a provider port. An invalid request must not accidentally create a billed session.','The route uses the shared Zod schema, returns a structured error when parsing fails, and only then proceeds to the bounded run. The SSE host supplies ordered frames and handles the response connection.', ['server/concepts/01-query.ts','server/sse.ts','shared/lab01-events.ts'],[2])
detail(5,'Both modes implement the Lab01Port interface.<br><br>Offline: authored deterministic events.<br><br>Live: real SDK calls, configuration checks and billing.', 'if (mode === "live") {\n  port = livePort();\n} else {\n  port = createFixturePort(\n    scenario, fixtureStepMs);\n}','server/concepts/01-query.ts · branch excerpt; error handling omitted','The run logic works through a port interface. Offline fixtures and live calls implement the same operations, so much of the event processing can be exercised without a provider session.','The route selects the port from the requested mode. Fixture scenarios are offline teaching cases. They are not provider measurements, and choosing an offline error scenario does not force the same failure in live mode.', ['server/concepts/01-query.ts','server/lib/lab01-port.ts','shared/lab01-events.ts'],[2])
detail(6,'Create a dedicated session.<br><br>Open its event stream before sending the prompt.<br><br>This ordering helps avoid missing events that arrive quickly.', 'session = await port.create();\nconst events = await raceAbort(\n  port.open(sessionId, upstream.signal),\n  local.signal);\nawait port.send(\n  sessionId, prompt, local.signal);','server/lib/lab01-run.ts · ordered excerpt; guards omitted','For a live run, the port delegates to the Anthropic SDK. It creates a session with the configured agent, environment, and session budget.','The runner awaits stream establishment before sending user dot message. The host then consumes provider events. Lab zero one expects a text-only agent; tool-enabled lessons need their own supported configuration.', ['server/lib/lab01-run.ts','server/lib/lab01-port.ts'],[2,3])
detail(7,'The event consumer separates previews, messages and lifecycle events.<br><br>Stop reason determines the turn outcome.<br><br>Cancellation uses a separate interrupt attempt and bounded cleanup.', 'const { frames, done } =\n  consumer.push(next.value);\nfor (const frame of frames) emit(frame);\nif (done) break;\n\n// Later: inspect status and archive\n// a settled session.','server/lib/lab01-run.ts · excerpt + explanatory comments','The consumer transforms provider events into typed frames. A preview can be replaced by its authoritative message. Lifecycle evidence determines completion rather than answer text alone.','After the turn, the runner checks status and attempts cleanup. If local waiting was cancelled or expired, it can send an independent interrupt request. It reports confirmed, unconfirmed, or pending states instead of assuming cleanup succeeded.', ['server/lib/session-events.ts','server/lib/lab01-run.ts'],[2,3])
detail(8,'The browser validates progress and the final result.<br><br>React renders agent text separately from lifecycle and outcome.<br><br>Students can inspect raw events and Result JSON.', 'const frame =\n  lab01FrameSchema.parse(data);\nsetFrames(current =>\n  [...current.slice(-299), frame]);\n\n// Final result is validated by\n// lab01ResultSchema in streamPost.','Concept01Query.tsx · excerpt + explanatory comments','The browser parses complete SSE frames, validates progress data, and updates React state. It also expects a validated terminal result, rather than treating a closed connection as success.','The interface shows session metadata, agent text, lifecycle events, and turn outcome as distinct evidence. Raw events and Result JSON help a student investigate when those pieces do not agree.', ['src/concepts/Concept01Query.tsx','src/lib/sse.ts','shared/lab01-events.ts'],[0])
add('Where the state lives',head('STATE AND PERSISTENCE','Learning progress is separate from execution history')+'<div class="grid">'+card('state-browser','Browser-local learning state','Checklists, notes and bookmarks<br>Knowledge-check attempts<br>Optional backup and restore')+card('state-host','Host-side state','Run controllers and limits<br>Lesson-specific stores and artifacts<br>Narration caches where configured')+card('state-cloud','Remote session state','Managed session identity and history<br>Provider lifecycle and events<br>Cleanup and archive status')+'</div><div class="banner"><p>Storage varies by lesson. The core learning interface does not require a universal cloud database.</p></div>',[('state-browser','Learning tools save supported progress in browser storage. This is not an account-based cloud sync service, and checklist completion is not proof of a successful live run.'),('state-host','The host maintains active run state and any lesson-specific stores or artifacts. The learning-guide endpoint also has a configured narration cache directory.'),('state-cloud','Managed session history belongs to the remote service. Archiving a session and backing up a student notebook are different operations. Always inspect the persistence model of the particular lab.')],['src/lib/learning-progress.ts','src/components/LearningBackupControls.tsx','server/index.ts','server/lib/lab01-run.ts'])
add('Configuration and trust boundaries',head('KEEP THE BOUNDARIES CLEAR','Configuration, credentials and readiness')+'<div class="two"><div class="card">'+cue('config-server','<h2>Server-only configuration</h2><p>Anthropic API key<br>Agent and environment IDs<br>Live gate, budget and deadlines</p>')+'</div><div class="card">'+cue('config-browser','<h2>Safe browser feedback</h2><p>Readiness and missing variable names<br>Validated data and bounded errors<br>No credential values</p>')+'</div></div><div class="banner">'+cue('config-levels','<p>Local readiness ≠ provider access verification ≠ a completed live run.</p>')+'</div>',[('config-server','Server configuration selects the resources and bounds execution. Keep credentials out of browser bundles, screenshots, and learning notes. Live mode requires its explicit gate and valid settings.'),('config-browser','The setup endpoint reports readiness and missing setting names. It does not send the secret values to the browser. Provider-facing errors are mapped to application messages.'),('config-levels','Distinguish three checks: local configuration readiness, a read-only provider access check, and a real completed live run. Each establishes something different.')],['server/lib/managed-config.ts','server/routes/managed.ts','vite.config.ts','scripts/managed-setup.ts'])
add('Verification and specialized labs',head('QUALITY AND EXTENSIBILITY','Test the core; verify integrations separately')+'<div class="grid">'+card('tests-core','Core checks','TypeScript type checking<br>Node offline tests<br>SSE parser and event-consumer tests')+card('tests-browser','Browser checks','Playwright UI tests<br>Navigation and exercise behavior<br>Isolated browser-test server ports')+card('tests-special','Specialized capabilities','MCP, WebSocket and observability labs<br>Cloud and integration adapters<br>Separate setup and live evidence')+'</div>',[('tests-core','The project checks TypeScript and uses Node tests for offline behavior. Stream parsing and event consumption deserve direct tests because partial data and lifecycle ordering matter.'),('tests-browser','Playwright checks the browser experience. Its test configuration uses separate ports and a controlled viewport, so test behavior can be reproduced.'),('tests-special','Later labs add capabilities such as MCP, WebSocket frontends, tracing, and cloud adapters. A dependency being installed does not mean its external service is configured or every live integration has been tested.')],['package.json','playwright.config.ts','tests/sse.test.ts'])
add('Architecture recap',head('YOUR MENTAL MODEL','Follow responsibilities, contracts and evidence')+'<div class="grid">'+card('recap-ui','Browser','Collect input<br>Display typed progress<br>Save local learning state')+card('recap-host','Host','Validate and coordinate<br>Own credentials and policies<br>Report outcomes and cleanup')+card('recap-runtime','Managed runtime','Execute the hosted agent session<br>Emit messages and lifecycle events<br>Maintain provider session state')+'</div><div class="banner"><p>Next: open Lab 01, trace /api/c1/query, and compare the fixture and live port implementations.</p></div>',[('recap-ui','Remember the three main responsibilities. The browser provides the learning experience and displays evidence.'),('recap-host','The host validates, coordinates, and reports what happened, including interruption and cleanup.'),('recap-runtime','The managed runtime executes the remote session. To continue, open Lab zero one, follow its request through the code, and compare the fixture port with the live port.')],['src/concepts/Concept01Query.tsx','server/lib/lab01-port.ts'])
